            <ArticleTitle>Anomalous origin of the right coronary artery from the left anterior descending coronary artery: a case report.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>915-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report on a 59-year-old man with effort angina of recent onset and a very uncommon right coronary artery originating from the middle portion of the left anterior descending; a tight stenosis of the left anterior descending coronary artery was also detected which involved the origin of the aberrant vessel.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
